# React Components Over HTML

Build UI with composable React components, not inline HTML in page files.

## Page Files

Page files (`app/**/page.tsx`) should compose components — not contain large blocks of markup.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — raw HTML in page
export default function Home() {
  return (
    <div>
      <div className="hero">...</div>
      <div className="services">...</div>
    </div>
  );
}

// ✅ GOOD — composed components
export default function Home() {
  return (
    <>
      <Hero />
      <ServicesGrid />
      <HowItWorks />
      <Testimonials />
      <ContactSection />
    </>
  );
}
```

## Component Rules

- Extract repeated UI into `components/ui/` (Button, Card, SectionHeading)
- Extract page sections into `components/sections/` (Hero, ServicesGrid, Footer)
- Use semantic HTML **inside** components: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<footer>`
- Use `next/link` for internal navigation, never raw `<a href="/...">`
- Props typed with TypeScript interfaces; avoid `any`
- Keep components focused — split if a file exceeds ~150 lines

## Client vs Server

- Default to Server Components (no `"use client"`)
- `"use client"` only when needed: EmailJS form, useState, useEffect, event handlers, browser APIs
